---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { COMMUNITY_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../config';
---

<Base title="About" current="about" description={`How ${SITE_NAME} works: where program details come from, how results are reported, and our promises.`}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="program-head">
      <h1>About {SITE_NAME}</h1>
      <p class="lead">A free home for everyone waiting to hear from graduate programs, wherever they are in the world.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        Every year, applicants rebuild the same spreadsheets to find out who has heard from which program. They break,
        they get locked, and they disappear when the season ends. {SITE_NAME} keeps that information in one place,
        organised by program, and keeps it from one year to the next.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is built by and for people who haven't made it yet: those who were rejected before, whose grades don't tell
        the whole story, or who are applying from far away without anyone to ask. Next comes {COMMUNITY_NAME}, a space
        to share what you've learned, find a supervisor and support each other.
      </p>

      <h2>Where program details come from</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every deadline, requirement and funding detail comes from the program's official pages, linked on each program page with the date we checked.</li>
        <li>If an official page doesn't say something, we write "Not stated on official pages". We never guess.</li>
        <li>Some programs are listed before we have checked their details, so you can follow them and report results. Their pages say "Details being checked" and link to the official page.</li>
        <li>Programs change details, so always confirm on the program's own site before you apply.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How results work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Anyone who signs in can report a result: an interview invitation, an offer, a waitlist place or a rejection.</li>
        <li>Results are anonymous. Others see the decision, the date and anything optional you add, never your name or email.</li>
        <li>When two or more people report the same decision for the same program within two days, each report shows that others reported it too.</li>
        <li>Anyone can flag a report as fake or harmful. A report flagged by three different people is hidden until a moderator checks it.</li>
        <li>"Applied" and "following" numbers count only people who use this site. They are not official totals.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our promises</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Results, deadlines and discussion stay free.</li>
        <li>We never sell personal information.</li>
        <li>We are not affiliated with any university, and we never promise admission.</li>
        <li>If we ever work with partners, they will be clearly labelled.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="corrections">Corrections and missing programs</h2>
      {
        CONTACT_EMAIL ? (
          <p>
            Found a mistake, or want a program added? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with
            a link to the official page.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            A contact address for corrections and missing programs is being set up. Until then, please check details on
            the program's official page.
          </p>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
